# MIR.DEV portfolio + contact API (Vercel-ready)

Static portfolio site + a small Express API (`api/index.js`) that emails
contact-form submissions through Nodemailer. Both deploy together on Vercel.

## Project layout

```
index.html, contact.html, ...   static site (served as-is)
style/, script/                 CSS and JS
api/index.js                    Express app -> Vercel serverless function
server.js                       local-only runner for the API
vercel.json                     routes /api/* to the Express app
.env.example                    environment variables to set
```

## Deploy on Vercel

1. Push this folder to GitHub (`.env` is git-ignored).
2. Vercel -> Add New Project -> import the repo. No build command or output
   directory is needed (Framework Preset: Other).
3. Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables, add (see `.env.example`):
   `SMTP_HOST`, `SMTP_PORT`, `SMTP_SECURE`, `SMTP_USER`, `SMTP_PASS`, `TO_EMAIL`
   (Gmail users: use an App Password from https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords).
4. Redeploy. Check `https://mir-dev.vercel.app/api/health` -> `{"status":"ok"}`.
5. Send a message from the contact page to test.

The frontend calls `/api/contact` on the same domain, so no CORS setup is needed.

## Run locally

```bash
npm install
cp .env.example .env     # fill in your SMTP values
npx vercel dev           # site + API together at http://localhost:3000
# or just the API:
npm run api              # http://localhost:5000/api/contact
```

Test it:

```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:5000/api/contact \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"name":"Test","email":"test@example.com","message":"Hello, testing!"}'
```

## Notes

- Validates name/email/message on the server; escapes HTML; blocks header injection.
- Rate limit is 5 messages / 15 min per IP. On serverless this is in-memory per
  instance (best effort). Use Upstash/Redis for strict limits.
- `replyTo` is the visitor's email, so Reply in your inbox goes straight to them.
- If the API fails, the form falls back to opening the visitor's email app.
